 <longdesc><para unique="1091450">The STTILECFG instruction takes a pointer to a 64-byte memory location (described in <link unique="1091446" linkend="&lt;c&gt;LDTILECFG-Load-Tile-Configuration.fm#77822: 06_Table: Table 2-1." xrefstyle="TableNum">Table 3&#8209;56</link> in the <link unique="1091449" linkend="&lt;c&gt;LDTILECFG-Load-Tile-Configuration.fm#89353: 05_Level: LDTILECFG&#8212;Load Tile Configuration" xrefstyle="SectionTitle">&#8220;LDTI&#173;LECFG&#8212;Load Tile Configuration&#8221;</link> entry) that will, after successful execution of this instruction, contain the descrip&#173;tion of the tiles that were configured. In order to configure tiles, the AMX_TILE bit in CPUID must be set and the operating system has to have enabled the tiles architecture.</para>
  <para unique="1091452">If the tiles are not configured, then STTILECFG stores 64B of zeros to the indicated memory location. </para>
  <para unique="1091453">Any attempt to execute the STTILECFG instruction inside an Intel TSX transaction will result in a transaction abort.</para>
  </longdesc>
 <operation>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1091455">STTILECFG 	mem</title>
   <programlisting>if TILES_CONFIGURED == 0:
	//write 64 bytes of zeros at mem pointer
	buf[0..63] := 0
	write_memory(mem, 64, buf)
else:
	buf.byte[0] := tilecfg.palette_id
	buf.byte[1] := tilecfg.start_row
	buf.byte[2..15] := 0
	p := 16
	for n in 0 ... palette_table[tilecfg.palette_id].max_names-1:
		buf.word[p/2] := tilecfg.t[n].colsb
		p := p + 2
	if p &lt; 47:
		buf.byte[p..47] := 0
	p := 48
	for n in 0 ... palette_table[tilecfg.palette_id].max_names-1:
		buf.byte[p++] := tilecfg.t[n].rows
	if p &lt; 63:
		buf.byte[p..63] := 0
	write_memory(mem, 64, buf)</programlisting>
   </section>
  </operation>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <programlisting>STTILECFG		void _tile_storeconfig(void *);</programlisting>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Flags Affected">
  <para unique="1091481" format="xIndent1">None.</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Exceptions">
  <para unique="1091486" format="xIndent1">AMX-E2; see <link unique="1091484" linkend="&lt;c&gt;__sdm_vol2A_ch02.fm#77014: 02_Level: 2.10 Intel&#174; AMX Instruction Exception Classes" xrefstyle="SectionNum&amp;Title(,)">Section 2.10, &#8220;Intel&#174; AMX Instruction Exception Classes,&#8221;</link> for details.</para>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
